<DocsLayout title="Observability" description="Understand project telemetry, host telemetry, logs, health signals, and MyPaaS fallback behavior.">
<section><p class="overline">Project telemetry</p><h2>Runtime metrics</h2><p>Running container-backed projects use a shared project metrics sampler. The preferred production path is <code>mypaas-statd</code> over its Unix socket; MyPaaS can fall back to the Docker-compatible metrics path when the statd runtime snapshot is unavailable.</p><DocMedia src={overviewShot} alt="MyPaaS project metrics overview" title="Project runtime metrics" source="MyPaaS dashboard" note="captured 13 Aug 2026" /><aside class="note"><p>Static projects do not have a persistent application runtime and therefore do not expose runtime CPU or memory telemetry.</p></aside></section>
<section><h2>Host telemetry</h2><p>The owner-only host statistics surface keeps host capacity and project allocation separate from live telemetry. With the current statd host-snapshot path, MyPaaS can report host CPU, memory, storage, and network telemetry without pretending that the API container namespace is the host.</p><DocMedia src={adminShot} alt="MyPaaS admin resource settings" title="Host and platform settings" source="MyPaaS dashboard" note="captured 13 Aug 2026" /></section>
<section><h2>Project logs</h2><p>Build output remains attached to deployment history. Runtime logs are read through the Docker-compatible command surface, and Compose logs retain service context.</p><DocMedia src={logsShot} alt="MyPaaS project logs view" title="Project logs" source="MyPaaS dashboard" note="captured 13 Aug 2026" /></section>
<section><h2>Control-plane health</h2><p>The API exposes <code>/health</code>, <code>/ready</code>, and Prometheus-compatible <code>/metrics</code>. Production verification also checks the statd service/socket when configured and the Caddy Admin Unix socket.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Surface</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>/health</code></td><td>Lightweight liveness.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/ready</code></td><td>Readiness and production verification.</td></tr><tr><td><code>/metrics</code></td><td>Control-plane process metrics with production authentication when configured.</td></tr></tbody></table></section>
<section><h2>What the dashboard does not claim</h2><p>MyPaaS does not fabricate historical telemetry from one current percentage. Runtime charts use bounded rolling samples collected while the view is active; host capacity and configured resource allocations remain separate concepts.</p></section>
</DocsLayout>
